note Exercism-style exercise "triangle": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/triangle
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note The sides a b c form a triangle when each is greater than 0 and the sum of any two is at least
note the third. equilateral: a triangle with all three sides equal; isosceles: a triangle with at
note least two sides equal; scalene: a triangle with all sides different.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/triangle
om2
fn istri a f64 b f64 c f64 to bool
if or or le a 0.0 le b 0.0 le c 0.0
ret false
end
ret and and ge add a b c ge add b c a ge add a c b
end
fn equilateral a f64 b f64 c f64 to bool
ret and istri a b c and eq a b eq b c
end
fn isosceles a f64 b f64 c f64 to bool
ret and istri a b c or or eq a b eq b c eq a c
end
fn scalene a f64 b f64 c f64 to bool
ret and istri a b c and and ne a b ne b c ne a c
end
